The ownership paths are clear: `AVDES` owns no pointers and can live inline or in an `av_malloc` allocation. `AVHMAC` owns a private hash context released by `av_hmac_free`; its allocator alone does not initialize the hash state, so the safe constructor will also initialize the key.
Both items match the type route. I’ll keep HMAC’s private fields opaque and expose DES’s public fields through copy-based accessors.
